WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.315
The creature's face disappeared into the bushes.

2
00:00:04.316 --> 00:00:07.188
The children bent over the caretaker.

3
00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:11.496
"He's not dead, is he?" Jimmy asked anxiously.

4
00:00:11.497 --> 00:00:17.820
"Just hurt," said Kathleen. "He's very handsome, don't you think?"

5
00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:21.067
"Oh yes," agreed Mabel.

6
00:00:21.068 --> 00:00:24.958
"Quite a nice young man," said a voice behind them.

7
00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:26.722
The children looked up.

8
00:00:26.723 --> 00:00:29.874
And there was the middle-aged Ugly-Wugly.

9
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:33.071
Everyone but Gerald screamed.

10
00:00:33.072 --> 00:00:36.883
He was still wearing the ring, so he wasn't afraid.

11
00:00:36.884 --> 00:00:40.258
But he noticed something strange.

12
00:00:40.259 --> 00:00:47.385
The middle-aged Ugly-Wugly's face was no longer made of paper—it was real.

13
00:00:47.386 --> 00:00:51.148
And so were his arms and legs.

14
00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.116
Somehow this creature had really come alive!

15
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:59.165
"What happened to the caretaker?" Gerald asked him.

16
00:00:59.166 --> 00:01:03.014
"It was most unfortunate," said the Ugly-Wugly.

17
00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:06.069
"The others must have lost their way in the passage last night.

18
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.456
They never found the hotel."

19
00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:12.500
"Did you find it?" Gerald said in surprise.

20
00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:19.739
"Of course. I wandered through the passage until I found the very nice hotel, just as you said.

21
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.213
When I found the others again, they were behind this door.

22
00:01:23.214 --> 00:01:24.508
They were angry.

23
00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:29.439
They'd been here all night, trying to get out."

24
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.408
Jimmy's eyes were wide with fear.

25
00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:36.896
"Here, take the ring," Gerald whispered.

26
00:01:36.897 --> 00:01:42.083
Jimmy put on the ring and instantly looked braver.

27
00:01:42.084 --> 00:01:48.674
"But what happened to the caretaker?" Gerald asked again.

28
00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.460
"He suddenly opened the door.

29
00:01:50.461 --> 00:01:53.816
Before I could protect him, the man in the top hat hit him.

30
00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:58.595
I was just going for help when you arrived."

31
00:01:58.596 --> 00:02:02.851
"We must find the others," said Gerald.

32
00:02:02.852 --> 00:02:07.157
"They've gone to bathe in the lake," said the Ugly-Wugly.

33
00:02:07.158 --> 00:02:11.534
"Their clothes are in the woods."

34
00:02:11.535 --> 00:02:15.725
Kathleen and Jimmy went to check on the other Ugly-Wuglies.

35
00:02:15.726 --> 00:02:20.183
Gerald and Mabel stayed behind to tend to the caretaker.

36
00:02:20.184 --> 00:02:24.364
The Ugly-Wugly sat down on the temple steps.

37
00:02:24.365 --> 00:02:28.288
In the woods Jimmy found four heaps of clothing.

38
00:02:28.289 --> 00:02:32.228
There were broomsticks, hockey sticks, and masks.

39
00:02:32.229 --> 00:02:35.779
All these things had made up the Ugly-Wugly men.

40
00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:40.359
Kathleen found the two ladies sitting on a bench in the sun.

41
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.885
But they had no life in them.

42
00:02:43.886 --> 00:02:54.225
Jimmy shook them to pieces.

43
00:02:54.226 --> 00:02:56.594
"The spell is broken."

44
00:02:56.595 --> 00:02:59.901
Kathleen sighed with relief.

45
00:02:59.902 --> 00:03:02.683
They went back to the Temple of Flora.

46
00:03:02.684 --> 00:03:05.433
The caretaker was trying to sit up.

47
00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:14.602
Gerald told the Ugly-Wugly to hide in the bushes so he wouldn't frighten the caretaker.

48
00:03:14.603 --> 00:03:18.940
"Jimmy is the best one to go with you," said Gerald.

49
00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:22.353
That was true because Jimmy had the ring.

50
00:03:22.354 --> 00:03:25.735
The children helped the caretaker to his feet.

51
00:03:25.736 --> 00:03:29.826
"Are you sure you're all right?" Mabel asked him.

52
00:03:29.827 --> 00:03:33.171
"Yes. But I had the strangest dream."

53
00:03:33.172 --> 00:03:36.583
He looked around.

54
00:03:36.584 --> 00:03:38.003
"I'm grateful for your help.

55
00:03:38.004 --> 00:03:40.600
You may visit here whenever you like."

56
00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:46.607
They all shook hands, and the caretaker walked away.

57
00:03:46.608 --> 00:03:51.318
"We have to get rid of that Ugly-Wugly," said Kathleen.

58
00:03:51.319 --> 00:03:54.503
"But how?" asked Gerald.

59
00:03:54.504 --> 00:03:56.859
"He became real inside the passage.

60
00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.028
If we could just get him back there . . ."

61
00:04:00.029 --> 00:04:03.695
Suddenly Jimmy came out of the bushes.

62
00:04:03.696 --> 00:04:08.187
"The Ugly-Wugly is taking a walk," Jimmy said.

63
00:04:08.188 --> 00:04:13.676
"He says he's a very rich businessman and he needs to get to London."

64
00:04:13.677 --> 00:04:18.240
Gerald and the girls were still planning how to get rid of the Ugly-Wugly.

65
00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:21.795
But Jimmy wasn't paying attention.

66
00:04:21.796 --> 00:04:24.774
"He has a car and a tennis court.

67
00:04:24.775 --> 00:04:27.933
I wish I were rich," said Jimmy.

68
00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.787
"I'd spend my money on . . ."

69
00:04:30.788 --> 00:04:35.234
"Oh no!" cried the girls, looking at Jimmy.

70
00:04:35.235 --> 00:04:39.092
Suddenly he was growing rich right in front of them.

71
00:04:39.093 --> 00:04:41.897
But he was also growing older.

72
00:04:41.898 --> 00:04:45.797
When the changes stopped, the girls gasped.

73
00:04:45.798 --> 00:04:54.756
"Do you know the way to the train station?" asked rich, old Jimmy.

